    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics has always been a mix of fascination and frustration for me. As a former high school student with an upper secondary education, I found it challenging but rewarding. I appreciate its logic and structure, especially in physics, but I struggle with advanced topics. My parents' backgrounds—my dad with a PhD and my mom with an upper secondary degree—helped me see math as both a tool and a language.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "Yes, anxiety about math often comes up when I face complex problems or new concepts. Growing up, I was encouraged to see math as a creative process rather than a rigid set of rules. However, as an older adult without formal higher education in math, I sometimes feel overwhelmed by abstract theories. My high neuroticism score reflects this tendency, making me more prone to stress when tackling unfamiliar material.",
    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "I tried a few AI tools last year for quick problem-solving and explanations, like a math chatbot that broke down equations step by step. It was helpful for basic algebra but less effective for advanced topics. Since I’m not a math expert, I found it frustrating when the AI gave overly technical answers without context. I’d recommend it for beginners but not for deep learning.",
